```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test and validate tenant isolation in a CI/CD pipeline?
- What failure modes would you anticipate when the DLQ grows large, and how would you mitigate them?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design autonomous, tenant-aware resilience in a distributed telemetry pipeline, emphasizing observability, per-tenant governance, and cross-region failure handling.

## Key Concepts

- OpenTelemetry integration across Kinesis → Lambda/Fargate → S3 → Glue/Athena
- Per-tenant SLAs guiding auto remediation and failover
- Exactly-once semantics with idempotent writes and deduplication
- Self-healing, circuit breakers, and backpressure to prevent cascading outages

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal idempotent writer for deduplication
async function writeEvent(event, store){
  const id = event.dedupToken;
  if (await store.exists(id)) return;
  await store.put(id, event.payload);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you simulate regional outages and verify auto-remediation?
- How would you measure SLA compliance per tenant and tune shard allocation?

## Why This Is Asked
Privacy and compliance demand masking at ingestion, not post-hoc. The candidate should design an isolation boundary for unmasked data, ensure per-tenant access controls, and plan end-to-end lifecycle.

## Key Concepts
- Ingestion-time PII masking with tenant isolation
- Per-tenant KMS keys and IAM-based access controls
- Dual data stores: masked data in a shared lake and unmasked in a restricted vault
- Glue catalog and Athena for querying masked data; DynamoDB for audit trails
- Data lifecycle and testing strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
function maskPII(record, tenantKey) {
  // pseudo-implementation
  record.phone = redact(record.phone);
  record.name = redact(record.name);
  return record;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate masking correctness at scale?
- What are the latency and cost trade-offs of this approach?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of cross-region data governance, policy-based routing, and end-to-end observability in AWS DVA pipelines. It also probes idempotency, late data handling, and LocalStack testing.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-region data movement and access control
- PII handling with encrypted destinations
- Idempotent writes (deviceId+timestamp)
- Late-arriving data strategies
- Observability with OpenTelemetry across services
- LocalStack testing plan for end-to-end validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-Lambda outline for routing based on policy
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const policy = await getPolicy(event.deviceId); // from DynamoDB or policy store
  const targetBucket = policy.isPII ? 'pii-secured-bucket' : 'standard-bucket';
  await writeToS3(targetBucket, event);
  await upsertDeviceState(event.deviceId, event.ts);
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
